  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers and thunderstorms return Sunday with a \nsevere weather risk.\n\nA potent shortwave trough will round the base of a mid-level low \nnear James Bay and pass across the eastern Great Lakes Sunday. A \nsurface wave will make its way from the central Great Lakes to the \nSaint Lawrence Valley, sending a cold front through the region and \ngenerate a round of widespread showers and thunderstorms. Ahead of \nthe system, favorable moisture return with PWATs climbing to 1.5-\n1.75 inches, and daytime heating will help increase instability, \nwith current modeled values around 500-1000 J/kg, and 0-6 km bulk \nshear to 40-50 knots. With these ingredients, there's potential for \nstrong to severe storms to form along the frontal boundary Sunday \nafternoon and evening, with the main threats being strong to \ndamaging winds and hail. The greatest severe potential will be \ninland from the lakes.",
